      "created_at": "2020-09-15T19:40:59Z",
      "updated_at": "2020-09-15T19:40:59Z",
      "body": "> My issue is that logins are a privacy violation. I kinda expect all user data to be deleted if I tell it to delete all user data, especially websites I visit. Another option is include it in the delete browsing history but include an additional warning as you said about being very destructive\r\n\r\nI could be wrong, but Fenix doesn't save logins without asking - each login must explicitly be saved by the user. I don't see that as a \"privacy violation\", if users are explicitly saving something. ",
